# go:embed targets become byte-for-byte content baked into the built binary
# (prompt templates sent to LLM agents, or scripts executed via shebang) --
# their bytes must be deterministic across checkouts regardless of a given
# machine's core.autocrlf setting, so they are pinned to LF here. The same
# byte-exact requirement applies to golden test fixtures compared verbatim
# against literal \n-embedded expectations in Go source (planparser below).
